## 7. One-Minute Project Explanation

Findora is a Lost and Found platform that helps people find their lost belongings.

For example, if someone loses a mobile phone or wallet, they can report it on Findora. If another person finds that item, they can also upload a found-item report.

Our platform helps connect the owner and the finder through matching functionality.

Users can communicate with each other and verify ownership before returning the item.

The main goal of Findora is to make the lost-and-found process easier, faster, and more organized.

I developed this project to solve a real-world problem and improve my full-stack development skills.

## 8. Important Points to Remember

- Findora solves a real-world problem.
- It connects item owners and finders.
- It provides a centralized lost-and-found platform.
- It helps users search and match lost and found reports.
- It supports communication between users.
- It can be useful in colleges, offices, malls, and communities.
